// prism_ui_upload -- file drop zone, upload-list item, upload list, and image preview (prism/ui/,
// milestone MB.21): dropzone, file_item, file_list, preview. Every one is a COMPOSITION over the
// closed 22-primitive vocabulary (widget/), built directly through prism_arrange.nova and
// prism_content.nova -- no new PrismNodeKind anywhere in this file (PRISM_SPEC.md axiom A7). This
// is the Ant Design `Upload` family: a drag-and-drop target, the per-file row a caller renders once
// per item in-progress, the container those rows live in, and the thumbnail an image upload shows
// once it has a source to preview. No struct is introduced anywhere in this file, so the
// field-slot-collision prefixing question (reference_field_slot_collision_scales_with_imports.md)
// never arises here -- every function takes only primitives, `PrismNode`, `PrismUpStatus`, and one
// bare `list`.
//
// ── WHY THIS FILE DOES NOT IMPORT `prism_ui_kit` ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every other recent `ui/` module (`prism_ui_notice`, `prism_ui_timeline`, `prism_ui_sort`) imports
// `prism_ui_kit` and reaches for `prism_ui_icon_text`/`prism_ui_collect` wherever a shape happens to
// match. Checked here first, deliberately (CLAUDE.md: "does this already exist?"): `icon_text`
// produces `band[glyph, label]` as a SUB-node, but every shape this file must produce is a single
// FLAT container -- `prism_up_file_item`'s `band[glyph(status), label(name), label(size),
// label(status)]` is four flat siblings, not `band[band[glyph,label], label, label]`, and wrapping
// the first two through `icon_text` would silently change the item's depth from 2 to 3 and its
// count from 5 to 6. `prism_ui_collect`'s map-with-error-propagation shape doesn't fit either: this
// file's one list-validation loop (`prism_up_file_list`) needs to name the OFFENDING INDEX in its
// rejection (mirroring `prism_nt_list`/`prism_tl_timeline`/`prism_so_sortable`'s identical
// convention), and `prism_ui_collect`'s `for it in items` has no index to report. Importing a module
// with nothing genuine to call from it would be dead weight this codebase does not carry anywhere
// else (verified: zero zero-use imports exist in `prism/` today) -- so it stays out.
//
// ── WHY THE STATUS ENUM IS CLOSED AT EXACTLY 3 VALUES (UPLOADING / DONE / FAILED) ─────────────────
// A file's transfer state is a small, genuinely closed set for the purpose this widget serves: it
// is either still moving, has arrived, or did not. Ant Design's own `Upload` has a `removed` status
// too, but "removed" is a LIST-MEMBERSHIP fact (the item is gone from the caller's list), not a
// per-item render state a file row needs to depict while still on screen -- a removed file has
// nothing left to draw. Axiom A7's closed-vocabulary discipline (already applied to `PrismNodeKind`
// and `PrismIcon`) is repeated here: adding a 4th status without extending
// `prism_up_status_name`/`prism_up_status_icon`'s exhaustive matches is a compile error, never a
// silently-wrong render.
//
// ── WHY `prism_up_file_item` RENDERS STATUS AS *BOTH* AN ICON AND A TEXT LABEL ────────────────────
// A status conveyed by icon alone is a shape/color-only signal (WCAG 1.4.1: color/shape must never
// be the ONLY carrier of information) -- a screen reader has no way to announce "the icon looks like
// a chevron" as "still uploading". Rendering `prism_up_status_name(s)` as a fourth, ordinary label
// alongside the glyph costs one extra child and buys every non-visual consumer (screen reader, ANSI
// backend with a monochrome terminal) the same information sighted users get from the icon shape.
//
// ── WHY `prism_up_status_icon` MAPS Uploading -> ChevronUp, NOT Warning OR Minus ──────────────────
// The closed 12-icon set (`prism_content.nova`) has no literal "spinner"/"in-progress" glyph.
// `ChevronUp` was picked over `Warning` (already claimed by `prism_fb_severity_icon`/
// `prism_nt_dot`'s "something needs your attention" meaning -- reusing it here would make an
// in-progress upload look like an alert) and over `Minus` (already claimed by
// `prism_tl_status_icon`'s Pending -- an upload actively transferring is not the same idea as "not
// started yet"). `ChevronUp` reads as "going up / in motion", the closest fit the fixed set offers,
// and is not claimed by any other status meaning already established in this codebase.
//
// ── WHY `up_max_size` IS `int?`, NOT A DEFAULT-VALUED INT ──────────────────────────────────────────
// Same reasoning `prism_arrange.prism_gap(size: int?)` and `prism_nt_badge(nt_max: int?)` already
// established for their own optional bound: "no limit advertised" and "limit defaults to some
// magic number" are different facts, and a defaulted int can never represent the former. `None`
// means the dropzone shows no size line at all; `Some(n)` means a fourth label is appended showing
// it. The label deliberately prints the bare number ("Max size: 5"), not a guessed unit ("5 MB") --
// this function has no unit parameter, and inventing one would be a silent, unverifiable assumption
// about what the caller's `n` counts (bytes? megabytes? some app-specific chunk size?). The caller
// owns unit formatting; this widget only owns whether the line exists.
//
// ── WHY `up_accept`'S ELEMENT CHECK IS "IS IT A STRING", NOT "IS IT A NON-EMPTY EXTENSION" ────────
// `up_accept` is a bare `list` (not `list<string>` -- mirroring `prism_node.nova`'s own
// self-referential-generic caution, and every other bare-list parameter in this codebase's `ui/`
// layer), so each element is guarded with `is_string(...)`, naming the offending index and actual
// type on rejection -- exactly `prism_so_sortable`'s discipline for its own `so_items: list`. A
// blank string element (`""`) IS a string, so it passes this check and would render as a stray
// empty entry in the joined accept text; this is a caller-supplied-garbage case distinct from "not
// a string at all" and is left undetected here deliberately -- the task's contract for this
// function draws the line at "non-string in accept", not "meaningless accept entry", and this file
// does not silently expand its own validation surface past what it is asked to guarantee.
//
// ── WHY `prism_up_file_list` REJECTS AN EMPTY LIST RATHER THAN SUBSTITUTING AN EMPTY STATE ────────
// `prism_nt_list` (prism_ui_notice.nova) renders `prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_empty(...)` when its items
// list is empty, because a notification feed can legitimately BE empty as steady-state UI ("no
// notifications yet" is itself a real screen). An upload list is different: the widget a caller
// shows when there are zero files in flight is `prism_up_dropzone` itself -- the drop target IS the
// empty state for uploads, exactly like Ant Design's own `Upload` component never renders an empty
// file-list container before the first file exists. Rendering a second, redundant "no files" panel
// underneath an already-empty dropzone would be visual noise, not information, so this function
// rejects the empty case instead of inventing a message no caller asked this file to own.
//
// ── WHY `prism_up_preview` TAKES A MANDATORY, ALWAYS-VALIDATED `up_alt` (NOT `prism_ui_figure`'s
//    two-constructor split) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// `prism_ui_media.prism_ui_figure` / `prism_ui_figure_decorative` exist as TWO constructors because
// a figure's image can legitimately be purely decorative (a background flourish with nothing to
// announce) -- see that file's own header on why `alt: string?` defaulting to "" would hide that
// distinction. An upload preview has no decorative case: it always depicts a real file the caller
// is uploading, and that file always has a name worth announcing. A single constructor with a
// mandatory, non-empty `up_alt` is therefore not a shortcut -- it is the correct, narrower contract
// for a narrower problem, and it means a caller can never accidentally ship a preview thumbnail
// with no accessible name.
//
// PUBLIC API
//   Enum (closed, 3 values -- see header)
//     PrismUpStatus                                    UpUploading() UpDone() UpFailed()
//     prism_up_uploading() / prism_up_done() / prism_up_failed()          cross-module ctors
//     prism_up_status_name(s) -> string      exhaustive: "uploading" | "done" | "failed"
//     prism_up_status_icon(s) -> PrismIcon   exhaustive: ChevronUp | Check | Close
//   Components (all Result<PrismNode>; every one validates, none fails silently)
//     prism_up_dropzone(up_label: string, up_accept: list, up_max_size: int?)
//       -> stack[glyph(Plus), label(up_label), label("Accepts: " + joined up_accept), label(max)?]
//       up_accept: bare list<string> (extensions like ".png"), runtime-checked (see header).
//       rejects an empty up_label, an empty up_accept, a non-string up_accept element (named by
//       index and type), and a present-but-non-positive up_max_size
//     prism_up_file_item(up_name: string, up_size_text: string, up_status: PrismUpStatus)
//       -> band[glyph(status icon), label(up_name), label(up_size_text), label(status name)]
//       rejects an empty up_name or up_size_text
//     prism_up_file_list(items: list) -> stack(items)
//       items: bare list<PrismNode>, runtime-checked. rejects an empty items list (see header --
//       the dropzone is the empty state, not this function) and a non-PrismNode element (named by
//       index and actual type)
//     prism_up_preview(up_name: string, up_alt: string, up_source: string)
//       -> stack[art(up_source) carrying an "alt" attr, label(up_name)]
//       rejects an empty up_name, an empty up_alt (a11y -- see header), and an empty up_source
//       (propagated from prism_content.prism_art unchanged)

import prism_node
import prism_arrange
import prism_content

// ── Status: closed, 3 values (see header) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
enum PrismUpStatus
    UpUploading()
    UpDone()
    UpFailed()

fn prism_up_uploading() -> PrismUpStatus
    UpUploading()
fn prism_up_done() -> PrismUpStatus
    UpDone()
fn prism_up_failed() -> PrismUpStatus
    UpFailed()

// Exhaustive, no wildcard arm -- adding a 4th status without a case here is a compile error.
fn prism_up_status_name(s: PrismUpStatus) -> string
    match s
        UpUploading() => "uploading"
        UpDone() => "done"
        UpFailed() => "failed"

// Exhaustive, no wildcard arm. See header for why each status maps to the icon it does.
fn prism_up_status_icon(s: PrismUpStatus) -> PrismIcon
    match s
        UpUploading() => prism_content.prism_icon_chevron_up()
        UpDone() => prism_content.prism_icon_check()
        UpFailed() => prism_content.prism_icon_close()

// ── Reconstruction helper: attach an extra attr to an already-built node ────────────────────────
// Identical shape `prism_ui_media._prism_md_with_attrs` / `prism_ui_notice.prism_nt_item` /
// `prism_ui_calendar._prism_cal_with_attrs` already use: build the plain node through its normal
// constructor first, then decorate it via `dict_merge` + `prism_node_new`. Still an `art` node
// (`PrismNodeKind` untouched, axiom A7 holds), just carrying one extra fact (`alt`).
fn _prism_up_with_attrs(n: PrismNode, extra: dict) -> Result<PrismNode>
    let merged = dict_merge(n.attrs, extra)
    prism_node.prism_node_new(n.kind, merged, n.children, n.key)

// ── Drop zone ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// "Accepts: .png, .pdf, ..." -- joined with ", ", matching this codebase's existing join-for-display
// convention (`prism_look`'s legal-state list, `prism_theme`'s legal-role list).
fn _prism_up_accept_text(up_accept: list) -> string
    "Accepts: " + join(up_accept, ", ")

// `0`-or-`1`-element list, spliced with `...` -- the same optional-part shape
// `prism_nt_item._prism_nt_opt_part` / `prism_st_stat._prism_st_opt_part` already establish for an
// optional trailing fact. See header for why the printed text carries no invented unit.
fn _prism_up_max_size_part(up_max_size: int?) -> Result<list>
    match up_max_size
        None => ok([])
        Some(n) =>
            if n <= 0
                return err("prism_up_dropzone: up_max_size must be > 0, got " + str(n))
            let node = prism_content.prism_label("Max size: " + str(n))?
            ok([node])

fn prism_up_dropzone(up_label: string, up_accept: list, up_max_size: int?) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(up_label) == 0
        return err("prism_up_dropzone: up_label must not be empty")
    if len(up_accept) == 0
        return err("prism_up_dropzone: up_accept must not be empty")
    for idx, ext in up_accept
        if not is_string(ext)
            return err("prism_up_dropzone: up_accept[" + str(idx) + "] must be a string, got " + type_name(ext))
    let max_parts = _prism_up_max_size_part(up_max_size)?
    let icon_node = prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_content.prism_icon_plus())?
    let label_node = prism_content.prism_label(up_label)?
    let accept_node = prism_content.prism_label(_prism_up_accept_text(up_accept))?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([icon_node, label_node, accept_node, ...max_parts])

// ── Single file row in an upload list ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// See header for why status is rendered as both icon AND text.
fn prism_up_file_item(up_name: string, up_size_text: string, up_status: PrismUpStatus) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(up_name) == 0
        return err("prism_up_file_item: up_name must not be empty")
    if len(up_size_text) == 0
        return err("prism_up_file_item: up_size_text must not be empty")
    let icon_node = prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_up_status_icon(up_status))?
    let name_node = prism_content.prism_label(up_name)?
    let size_node = prism_content.prism_label(up_size_text)?
    let status_node = prism_content.prism_label(prism_up_status_name(up_status))?
    prism_arrange.prism_band([icon_node, name_node, size_node, status_node])

// ── Upload list (the container `prism_up_file_item` rows live in) ──────────────────────────────
// `items` is a bare `list` (not `list<PrismNode>` -- mirroring `prism_node.nova`'s own
// self-referential-generic caution, and `prism_nt_list`'s/`prism_tl_timeline`'s identical choice
// for the identical reason), so every element is guarded with the same `type_name(...) !=
// "PrismNode"` check, naming the offending index and actual type on rejection. See header for why
// an empty list is a rejection here, not a substituted empty state.
fn prism_up_file_list(items: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(items) == 0
        return err("prism_up_file_list: items must not be empty -- render prism_up_dropzone instead when there are no files in flight")
    for idx, it in items
        if type_name(it) != "PrismNode"
            return err("prism_up_file_list: item " + str(idx) + " is not a PrismNode (got " + type_name(it) + ")")
    prism_arrange.prism_stack(items)

// ── Image preview thumbnail ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// See header for why `up_alt` is mandatory here rather than the two-constructor split
// `prism_ui_figure`/`prism_ui_figure_decorative` use. Empty-source rejection is
// `prism_content.prism_art`'s own, propagated unchanged.
fn prism_up_preview(up_name: string, up_alt: string, up_source: string) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(up_name) == 0
        return err("prism_up_preview: up_name must not be empty")
    if len(up_alt) == 0
        return err("prism_up_preview: up_alt must not be empty -- an upload preview with no accessible name is an a11y defect")
    let art_node = prism_content.prism_art(up_source)?
    let art_with_alt = _prism_up_with_attrs(art_node, {"alt": up_alt})?
    let name_node = prism_content.prism_label(up_name)?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([art_with_alt, name_node])
